<title>PHILIPPINES: Petron up 8.25 pct on deregulation news.</title>
<headline>Petron up 8.25 pct on deregulation news.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil refiner Petron Corp surged by 80 centavos, or 8.25 percent, to 10.50 pesos on Thursday on news that President Fidel Ramos approved the implementation of full oil industry deregulation a month ahead of schedule.</p>
<p>&quot;It's always been a consensus that Petron will benefit from full deregulation and the major reason is that it now has full latitude to increase its profits,&quot; said Raul Ruiz, vice-president at Sun Hung Kai Securities.</p>
</text>
